{"title":"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Hint\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Hint</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_(inversions)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution (inversions)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_(trig_bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution (trig bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies between the rays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0964c9cf406ef8e5ec8beaa6a92125f2d8f90460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0964c9cf406ef8e5ec8beaa6a92125f2d8f90460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> collinear with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/879556cdd4808764a2b68b789e3edd0bf04ccd2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{PQ} + \\frac{1}{PR}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"85\" height=\"40\" /> is as large as possible.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Hint\">Hint</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Hint\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are two ways to solve this problem. The first is more subtle, and the second is just bashing.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_.28inversions.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_(inversions)\">Solution (inversions)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution (inversions)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Perform the inversion with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/55550a50a8e0892d393cba83f10de79553456e9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PO}.$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" /> Lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a79f5f7511b74da0df00953948d2f52ecb6d745.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA,OB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> go to the circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bb1e90fc02d8c9be08bc40b8e8a11780c935c65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(O_1),(O_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/9/4c97d3c4cd71e70792477618fae9df724e9be8e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> and the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> cuts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bb1e90fc02d8c9be08bc40b8e8a11780c935c65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(O_1),(O_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> again at the inverses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b21440cb0e17dea6cb522898391be18dfc61e5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q&#39;,R&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/40946d157b5830585dfb3a49764dcafaac5a6deb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q,R.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> Hence\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7abbd72ed1c4c875d4c5f0c455c8a0993994118a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{PQ}+\\frac{1}{PR}=\\frac{PQ&#39;+PR&#39;}{PO^2}=\\frac{Q&#39;R&#39;}{PO^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"267\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Thus, it suffices to find the line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> that maximizes the length of the  segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/3/3f366b0d63618e165d8ea21c034b7d40b5a1a335.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{Q&#39;R&#39;}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"19\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e929dc6c21edf7f11254db489376105e0abc1b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M,N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> are the midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d38b07e0d558f9456280930556558a0a10b6a09d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ&#39;,PR&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" /> i.e. the projections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba052c588c8b07084bc97066e611011e0514e4df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1,O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/3/5235db464e4e5eb3f31e8e11dca4e40a0e121ce0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" /> then from the right trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d6a20f486a9bd83d8276632c83bf13c8948e57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1O_2NM,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" /> we deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa68b238ae6c17cda7e339d05c74e985ef6632e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1O_2 \\ge MN = \\frac{_1}{^2}Q&#39;R&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"180\" height=\"24\" /> Consequently, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/fae2ded4007df6048f0a3e405d8dbeb1011bf2b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot O_1O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" /> is the greatest possible length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccd43c3fe38e543e4454954ae9357a8963256f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q&#39;R&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> which obviously occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f9f04fa7ecbdb07aaf22f3ee24adf283112b39e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1O_2NM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" /> is a rectangle. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/3/9d31d38379af3b22ed3610dd35bbc37bd55cabb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q,R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> are the intersections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a79f5f7511b74da0df00953948d2f52ecb6d745.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA,OB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> with the perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/f/25fe9bf59f0b24dfa18ae578c071f8fffaf7c7fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3ce33ec2a34dc4fddaec3224043f4a72bbe6d0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_.28trig_bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_(trig_bash)\">Solution (trig bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution (trig bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/6/126a7c3e9905b7f17abee0f8eca9ea02e78c95f4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair O = (0,0), A = (14,28), Q = (20,40), B = (16,0), R = (25,0), P = (23,16); dot(O); dot(A); dot(Q); dot(B); dot(R); dot(P); label(&quot;O&quot;, O, S); label(&quot;A&quot;, A, W); label(&quot;Q&quot;, Q, W); label(&quot;B&quot;, B, S); label(&quot;R&quot;, R, S); label(&quot;P&quot;, P, E); draw(O--R--Q--O); draw(O--P); label(&quot;r&quot;, O--P, N); [/asy]\" width=\"158\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75d6eda3ba5d364f220e5ed9510f89f1d47cc132.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = OP, x = \\angle OPR, a = \\angle POR,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"259\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08af2b1c1d1d8f9d74c1e471cfb38366a5fb8bde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\angle POQ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/d/3cdc2d1607c4102cc5bdba51fdb29d3d4394fc58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ORP = \\pi - x - a$\" width=\"155\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae75f8c509aaf9e2eb62cfdf6585150ddd51cf3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OQP = x - b.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" /> Using the Law of Sines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/0/5a04fe550dfa8feb59541771554ac81babd36eec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OPR$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/71058985a39467316ac4c1b374f4bd049cfe10a4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PR = \\sin a * \\frac{r}{\\sin(\\pi - x - a)} = \\sin a * \\frac{r}{\\sin(x + a)},\\]\" width=\"383\" height=\"37\" />\nand using the Law of Sines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dd05513c1a170b4f2356d5efe4ece31cf814845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OPQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c6201da87f5fc3ad883710472a1f0cc9614cf1a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PQ = \\sin b * \\frac{r}{\\sin(x - b)}.\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"37\" />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/80303c201846c205179a6b3f6e27ecd39abb3174.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r, a,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are given constants.\nHence,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba92e7ef8c000e3ed97b05ded6d9ca9e9dbf696.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{PR} + \\frac{1}{PQ} = \\frac{1}{r} (\\frac{\\sin(x + a)}{\\sin a} + \\frac{\\sin(x - b)}{\\sin b}) = \\frac{\\sin(x+a)\\sin b + \\sin(x-b)\\sin a}{r \\sin a \\sin b} = \\frac{\\sin x\\cos a\\sin b + \\sin a\\cos x\\sin b + \\sin x\\cos b\\sin a - \\cos x\\sin b\\sin a}{r \\sin a \\sin b} = \\frac{\\sin x(\\sin b \\cos a + \\sin a \\cos b)}{r \\sin a \\sin b}\\]\" width=\"1373\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Clearly, this quantity is maximized when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd0a9812463f356356a99fbdc2ddfc21f36a7f30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x = 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"12\" /> Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/879556cdd4808764a2b68b789e3edd0bf04ccd2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{PQ} + \\frac{1}{PR}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"85\" height=\"40\" /> is as large as possible when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/5573c85fbc1e06c23593e7e0d8009d465b06e6f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{\\pi}{2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"33\" /> or when line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> is perpendicular to line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/f/25fe9bf59f0b24dfa18ae578c071f8fffaf7c7fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO\" title=\"1979 USAMO\">1979 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1979\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017041625\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.069 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 313/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1267/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10067/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   26.392      1 -total\n 77.67%   20.499      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 21.49%    5.672      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10086:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017041625 and revision id 93149. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}